619 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Eligibility Criteria for Drone Pilot Training Not everyone can operate a drone commercially in India. To obtain a Remote Pilot Certificate \(RPC\), an individual must meet the following criteria: Minimum Age Requirement: The applicant must be at least 18 years old and not older than 65 years at the time of application. Educational Qualification: A minimum qualification of Class 10 \(Matriculation\) or equivalent from a recognized board. Medical Fitness: The applicant should be physically and mentally fit to operate a drone safely. Medical Fitness Certificate should be duly signed by a Medical Practitioner  Enrollment in a DGCA-Approved Remote Pilot Training Organization \(RPTO\): Only RPTOs authorized by the DGCA can provide drone pilot training and issue RPCs. Link for RPTOS)
/E (Eligibility Criteria for Drone Pilot Training Not everyone can operate a drone commercially in India. To obtain a Remote Pilot Certificate \(RPC\), an individual must meet the following criteria: Minimum Age Requirement: The applicant must be at least 18 years old and not older than 65 years at the time of application. Educational Qualification: A minimum qualification of Class 10 \(Matriculation\) or equivalent from a recognized board. Medical Fitness: The applicant should be physically and mentally fit to operate a drone safely. Medical Fitness Certificate should be duly signed by a Medical Practitioner  Enrollment in a DGCA-Approved Remote Pilot Training Organization \(RPTO\): Only RPTOs authorized by the DGCA can provide drone pilot training and issue RPCs. Link for RPTOS)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
