/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Chapter 7: Specific Operation Risk Assessment \(SORA\) The Specific Operation Risk Assessment \(SORA\) is a structured methodology developed by JARUS \(Joint Authorities for Rulemaking on Unmanned Systems\) to assess and mitigate risks in drone operations. It is essential for ensuring the safety of operations, particularly in Visual Line of Sight \(VLOS\) and Beyond Visual Line of Sight \(BVLOS\) scenarios. SORA identifies potential risks to people, property, and other airspace users, requiring operators to implement mitigation strategies. In VLOS operations, risks are lower but still demand compliance with local regulations. For BVLOS operations, SORA becomes crucial to address higher risks, such as communication failures or mid-air collisions.)
/E (Chapter 7: Specific Operation Risk Assessment \(SORA\) The Specific Operation Risk Assessment \(SORA\) is a structured methodology developed by JARUS \(Joint Authorities for Rulemaking on Unmanned Systems\) to assess and mitigate risks in drone operations. It is essential for ensuring the safety of operations, particularly in Visual Line of Sight \(VLOS\) and Beyond Visual Line of Sight \(BVLOS\) scenarios. SORA identifies potential risks to people, property, and other airspace users, requiring operators to implement mitigation strategies. In VLOS operations, risks are lower but still demand compliance with local regulations. For BVLOS operations, SORA becomes crucial to address higher risks, such as communication failures or mid-air collisions.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
