/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Scenario 1: Mapping in a Semi-Urban Area Operation: A drone service provider is tasked with mapping a semi-urban area for a local municipality. Risk Assessment: Ground Risk: Presence of residential areas increases risk to people on the ground. Air Risk: Nearby helipads or manned aviation corridors could pose a collision risk. Mitigation Measures: Perform operations during low-activity hours. Use Geo-fencing and Return-to-Home features. Issue public notifications and barricade the operational area.)
/E (Scenario 1: Mapping in a Semi-Urban Area Operation: A drone service provider is tasked with mapping a semi-urban area for a local municipality. Risk Assessment: Ground Risk: Presence of residential areas increases risk to people on the ground. Air Risk: Nearby helipads or manned aviation corridors could pose a collision risk. Mitigation Measures: Perform operations during low-activity hours. Use Geo-fencing and Return-to-Home features. Issue public notifications and barricade the operational area.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
715 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Scenario 2: Aerial Inspection of Power Lines in a Red Zone Operation: A drone operator is hired to inspect power lines in a Red Zone, requiring ATC, AAI, and DGCA approval. Risk Assessment: Ground Risk: Proximity to critical infrastructure heightens risk. Air Risk: Red Zone classification indicates restricted airspace. Mitigation Measures: Submit a detailed flight plan to DigitalSky. Use a TC-certified drone with failsafe features. Deploy a trained observer team to monitor hazards.)
/E (Scenario 2: Aerial Inspection of Power Lines in a Red Zone Operation: A drone operator is hired to inspect power lines in a Red Zone, requiring ATC, AAI, and DGCA approval. Risk Assessment: Ground Risk: Proximity to critical infrastructure heightens risk. Air Risk: Red Zone classification indicates restricted airspace. Mitigation Measures: Submit a detailed flight plan to DigitalSky. Use a TC-certified drone with failsafe features. Deploy a trained observer team to monitor hazards.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [0]
